  "reasoning": "The patient presents with high fever, weakness, and significant muscle pain. These symptoms align closely with dengue fever, often characterized by severe body aches (breakbone fever), fatigue, and fever. Other options like malaria typically involve chills and sweating cycles; common cold involves respiratory symptoms; bronchial asthma involves breathing difficulties; and typhoid involves abdominal pain. The absence of these specific differentiating symptoms points to dengue as the most likely diagnosis.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]dengue[/DIAGNOSIS]"
